<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Pascoe Fawkner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1792–1869</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Pascoe Fawkner was an Australian pioneer, businessman and politician who helped found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melbourne">Melbourne</a> in 1835. Raised in Van Diemen's Land, he sent a party on the schooner Enterprize to the Yarra River in 1835 and soon settled there himself. He opened Melbourne's first hotel and published its first newspaper, and later served in Victoria's Legislative Council.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-pascoe-fawkner.jpg" alt="John Pascoe Fawkner" width="320" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patterson Bros. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Pascoe_Fawkner_1862_SLNSW_FL3281745.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
